PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — opt-in adaptive meshing through a new export,
Mesh_hCreateFromVoxelsAdaptive. Upstreamable to leap71/PicoGKRuntime; not yet
offered.

Applied to vendor/PicoGKRuntime by scripts/fetch-deps.sh after 0001-0005.
Kept as a patch because it modifies dependency source; no flag-level override
exists.

1. Source/PicoGKVdbVoxels.h — roAsMesh() gains fAdaptivity (default 0) and
   bRelax (default false). At 0 the call is the one 0001 makes,
   VolumeToMesh(0, 0, false) with enableFlatQuadOutput(), so
   Mesh_hCreateFromVoxels keeps its bytes. Above 0 it runs
   VolumeToMesh(0, fAdaptivity, bRelax): OpenVDB's adaptive mesher merges
   near-coplanar cells, and bRelax turns on its relaxDisorientedTriangles pass.
   OpenVDB runs that pass only when meshing is adaptive (VolumeToMesh.h,
   `adaptive && mRelaxDisorientedTriangles`), so bRelax changes nothing at 0.
   The adaptive branch never takes the flat-quad path (VolumeToMesh selects it
   only for uniform, non-reference meshing), so the result is read through
   0001's per-leaf pool path, triangles and quads.
2. API/PicoGK.h, Source/PicoGKLibrary.cpp — Mesh_hCreateFromVoxelsAdaptive
   (hInstance, hVoxels, fAdaptivity, bRelax): NaN and values at or below 0
   select the uniform mesher; values at or above 1 clamp to the largest float
   below 1. At 1 OpenVDB stops comparing normals (`useGradients = adaptivity <
   1`) and merges on topology alone, a different algorithm rather than a
   coarser setting of the same one.

Evidence: adaptivity sweep 2026-10-22 (Tau Brain), relax off recommended: it
never changes triangle count or topology and lowers vertex deviation.
